<title>THAILAND: Thai grains discharge schedule for May 6.</title>
<headline>Thai grains discharge schedule for May 6.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shippers and surveyors detailed grains discharges at Thai ports as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	   Date of Arrival    Commodity	     Amount</p>
<p>Da Xiang	    Apr  07	   IND rapseed	    5,444</p>
<p>					    IND groundnut meal   5,685</p>
<p>Sin Hung 2	  Apr 19	    IND groundnut meal     964</p>
<p>					    IND soymeal	    5,798</p>
<p>Pacific King	Apr 10	    US soybeam	    39,791</p>
<p>Sohret		Apr 13	    IND rapeseed	   6,583</p>
<p>Varva		 Apr 15	    US soybean	    16,798</p>
<p>					    US corn gluten	 3,811</p>
<p>					    US fertilizers	 6,298</p>
<p>Menities	    Apr 15	    US soymeal	    36,019</p>
<p>					    US soybean	    16,041</p>
<p>Pretty Flourish   Apr 20	    CAN canola meal	6,452</p>
<p>Pingquan	    N/A		 IND soymeal	    4,000</p>
<p>					    IND groundnut meal     600</p>
<p>					    IND rapeseed	   3,000</p>
<p>Rodisi		May 15	    ARG corn		36,250</p>
<p>					    BRZ soymeal(hi-pro) 13,000</p>
<p>					    BRZ soymeal(lo-pro)  6,500</p>
<p>Tascana	     May 10	    ARG soybean	    7,600</p>
<p>					    ARG soy pellets     22,400</p>
<p>					    ARG sun pellets     19,000</p>
<p>Vita Spa	    N/A		 BRZ soybean	   50,000</p>
<p>Note: IND=India, ARG = Argentina, AUS=Australia, US = United States, BRZ=Brazil, CAN = Canada.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
